## 2026-09-16 — 22:55 IST

### Fixed: stale DB check constraints blocking media upload (room_tag, property_type)

Why: After property publish succeeded, uploading a tagged media asset failed with a 500 error. The backend log showed: `ERROR: new row for relation "property_media_assets" violates check constraint "property_media_assets_room_tag_check"`. The failing value was `GENERAL`.

Root cause: Same pattern as the `latitude NOT NULL` issue. PostgreSQL check constraints are created once and `ddl-auto: update` never modifies them. Two enums were extended after the constraint was originally created:
- `RoomTag` enum now has 10 values (`GENERAL`, `MASTER_BEDROOM`, `BATHROOM` added later), but the DB constraint only listed the original 7.
- `PropertyType` enum now has 7 values (`PENTHOUSE`, `STUDIO`, `SERVICED_APARTMENT` added later), but the DB constraint only listed the original 4.

Files affected:
- PostgreSQL DB schema only — `property_media_assets` and `listings` tables. No Java source files changed.

What changed:
- Dropped `property_media_assets_room_tag_check` and recreated with all 10 current `RoomTag` values: `GENERAL`, `LIVING_ROOM`, `MASTER_BEDROOM`, `BEDROOM`, `KITCHEN`, `BATHROOM`, `BALCONY`, `EXTERIOR`, `AMENITIES`, `FLOOR_PLAN`.
- Dropped `listings_property_type_check` and recreated with all 7 current `PropertyType` values: `FLAT`, `HOUSE`, `PLOT`, `LAND`, `PENTHOUSE`, `STUDIO`, `SERVICED_APARTMENT`.
- Audited `listings_listing_type_check`, `listings_status_check`, `property_media_assets_media_type_check` — all confirmed matching their enums (no action needed).

Verification:
- `pg_get_constraintdef` confirmed both constraints now include all enum values.
- `ListingStatus` (3 values), `MediaType` (4 values) — constraints verified clean.

Commit status:
- DDL-only fix applied directly to local DB. No Java source files changed. If Flyway/Liquibase is adopted, capture both constraint migrations.
